% UPDATED APPROACH
\sectiontitle{Updated Project Approach and Architecture (2 pts)}

\vspace{0.05cm}

\instruction{
}

\vspace{0.25cm}

\answerbox{9.85cm}{The system is divided into three layers with a strict separation between them.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{1. Persistence layer (database.h)} --- a Database class wrapping the SQLite C API. It manages four
tables: tasks (task details, ideal and minimum time, mandatory and needs-going-out flags), day\_plan (minutes
allocated to each task on a date), settings (wake-up time) and commitments (weekly college or work hours).
Plans are saved inside a transaction, and older databases are upgraded automatically with ALTER TABLE without
losing data.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{2. Logic layer} --- scheduler.cpp (compression and task-dropping), advisor.cpp (rule-based
suggestions and free-slot rules) and commitments.cpp (merging of busy time). This layer has no SQLite
dependency. It accepts plain structs and returns results, so every algorithm is tested without a database.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{3. Interface layer} --- main.cpp (menu-driven CLI) and gui.cpp (desktop GUI with What now, Plan my
day, Tasks and My schedule tabs). Both call the same logic functions, so they always give the same answer.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{Own DSA library (dsa.h):} DynArray (growable array), BinaryHeap (priority queue stored in an array)
and mergeSort replace std::vector, std::priority\_queue and std::sort. The heap selects which task to drop
and ranks suggestions; merge sort orders busy intervals before they are merged.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{Communication:} the application runs fully offline and uses no network protocol or external API. The
two interfaces communicate only through the shared SQLite file and the shared engine.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{Libraries and tool chain:} C++17; SQLite (amalgamation compiled into the program); Dear ImGui 1.91.6
with GLFW and OpenGL 3 for the GUI, kept in third\_party/; g++ 15.2 on Ubuntu under WSL with -Wall; VS Code;
DB Browser for SQLite; and Git/GitHub for version control.}

