% CHALLENGES
\sectiontitle{Challenges/Roadblocks (7 pts)}

\vspace{0.05cm}

\instruction{

}

\vspace{0.18cm}

\answerbox{8.40cm}{\textbf{1. Antivirus software blocked every Windows build.} McAfee deleted the compiled
program each time MinGW produced it, so nothing could be run. Resolved by moving the build to Ubuntu under
WSL, where the same code compiles with g++ without interference.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{2. The GUI library did not compile with the newer compiler.} Dear ImGui 1.91.6 failed to build with
GCC 15 because of a missing header. Resolved by adding the compiler flag -include cstring.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{3. A new database column had to be added without losing user data.} The needs\_outside field did not
exist in databases created earlier. Resolved by checking the table's columns at startup and adding the column
with ALTER TABLE. An old database was tested to confirm that no row was lost.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{4. Two separate Git histories had to be combined.} The shared repository and the local project were
created separately, so a normal push was refused. Resolved by merging both histories and checking that only
the report and README were added to the code.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{5. Replacing the STL without changing any result.} Writing our own dynamic array, heap and sort could
introduce small errors. Resolved by running the old and new versions on 60,000 random inputs and confirming
that the output was identical.

\vspace{3pt}
\textbf{6. Daily routines and start times are still not modelled.} Sleep is identified by its name, and the
plan does not give each task a start time. Planned resolution: a separate routines table and a fixed\_start
column.}

